      <span class="section-label">Summary</span>
      <h2>Key Takeaways</h2>

      <div class="takeaway-grid">
        <div class="takeaway-card">
          <h4>Prompt Engineering</h4>
          <p>Systematic design of prompts to guide model responses. Quality prompts directly improve response quality, making this a critical skill.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="takeaway-card">
          <h4>Clarity and Specificity</h4>
          <p>Be explicit about what you want. Specify format, length, audience, and constraints. Vague prompts produce vague results.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="takeaway-card">
          <h4>RCFC Framework</h4>
          <p>Role, Context, Format, Constraints. This structure provides maximum guidance to models and improves response quality consistently.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="takeaway-card">
          <h4>Iterative Refinement</h4>
          <p>Start simple, evaluate results, identify gaps, refine iteratively. Document successful patterns for reuse across projects.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="takeaway-card">
          <h4>Examples Matter</h4>
          <p>Providing examples (few-shot prompting) dramatically improves response quality. Models learn from examples better than from instructions alone.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="takeaway-card">
          <h4>API Parameters</h4>
          <p>Temperature controls creativity (0=deterministic, 1=creative). Max_tokens controls length. Top_p controls diversity. Tune for your task.</p>
        </div>
